# cicada 1
# B-rep solids — the default working mode (DECISIONS.md row 42): a box, a
# sphere, a solid_difference in the OCCT kernel, measured, tessellated once
# at the end for the debug OBJ exporter.
# Solve only:        cargo run -p cicada-cli -- run examples/02-solids.cic
# Write the OBJ:     cargo run -p cicada-cli -- run examples/02-solids.cic --node dump
# (exporters are effectful: they NEVER run unless named with --node)
# The mesh tier (Manifold) is still here under mesh_* names — see
# 03-voronoi.cic for a carve that stays on meshes.

# Scrub-cached (v0.1 item 5): the 19 positions of 0.5…5.0 by 0.25 are
# pre-solved while the app is idle, so dragging `size` later is a cache read.
size = slider(value=2.0, min=0.5, max=5.0, step=0.25, scrub=True)
span = construct_domain(start=0.0, end=size)

# Solids are exact: the box is six planar faces, the ball one spherical one.
block = box(x=span, y=span, z=span)

# A ball poking through the block's top face...
top = construct_point(x=1.0, y=1.0, z=2.0)
top_frame = xy_plane(origin=top)
ball = sphere(plane=top_frame, radius=0.75)

# Geometry lists come from nodes (list literals hold plain scalars);
# duplicate(count=1) is the idiomatic singleton.
cutter_list = duplicate(item=ball, count=1)

# The carve, in the kernel; the result is still one exact solid.
carved = solid_difference(solid=block, cutters=cutter_list)

# Measure it — the numbers a mesh could only approximate.
carved_volume, carved_centroid = volume(solid=carved)

# Tessellate once, at the end, for the mesh-destined exporter.
shell = tessellate(solid=carved, deflection=0.01)
dump_list = duplicate(item=shell, count=1)
dump = export_obj(meshes=dump_list, path="02-solids.obj")
